.TH "__hhs_do" "1" "2026-03-26" "HomeSetup" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
__hhs_do - Execute a shell command sequence N times, continuing through failures.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
usage: __hhs_do <N> <command; command; ...>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute a shell command sequence N times. Each semicolon-delimited command is executed in order, even if a previous command in the same iteration fails.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
$1 (Req)
Number of times to repeat the command sequence.
.TP
$2..$N (Req)
Shell commands separated by semicolons.
.SH DETAILS
.nf

    Arguments:
      <N>        : Number of times to repeat the command sequence.
      <command>  : One or more shell commands separated by semicolons.

    Result:
      Non-zero return codes are recorded, but later commands in the sequence still run.

    Examples:
      __hhs_do 10 'pk -f Global; sleep 1; echo -n "."'
      __hhs_do 3 'echo one; echo two'
.fi
